-- title:
--   Supersingular prolongation with smooth-point charts, level q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 2$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\kappa$-field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set for $q$), and let $s \in W$. Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from the base-changed full level-$M'$ field to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` which is compatible with coefficientwise reduction: every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0$'s valuation subring and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise residue. Then there are a field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to `fieldBar q M'` with residue field $F_{ss}$ such that: (i) some element of $F_{ss}$ is transcendental over $\kappa$; (ii) for $f$ in $R_0$'s valuation subring whose order is non-negative at every place at which the $q$-expansion image of $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R$'s valuation subring and its $R$-residue is the image of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue; (iii) $R$'s valuation subring is invariant under pullback along each `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Moreover there are a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}/\kappa$ with $|N| = q+1$ and, for each place $Q$, a subring $S_Q$ of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring map $\varphi_Q \colon A[X] \to S_Q$, a character $\chi_{0,Q} \colon S_Q \to \kappa$ and a set $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that for every $Q \notin N$: $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified, sends constants to the corresponding elements of $A$, and satisfies $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a)) = \bar a$ and $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; for each $c \in A$ with $\bar c = 0$ there is exactly one ring map $S_Q \to A$ fixing the constants, lifting $\chi_{0,Q}$ and sending $\varphi_Q(X)$ to $c$; each element of $S_Q$ lies in $R$'s valuation subring with $R$-residue in $Q$'s valuation subring reducing to the image of $\chi_{0,Q}$ in $Q$'s residue field; $\varphi_Q(X)$ has $R$-residue of order $1$ at $Q$; $D_Q$ consists precisely of the rational places $P$ at which all elements of $S_Q$ are regular with values in $A$, the values of valuation $<1$ being exactly those on which $\chi_{0,Q}$ vanishes; every constant-fixing lift of $\chi_{0,Q}$ to $A$ is evaluation at a unique $P \in D_Q$; for $P \in D_Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_Q$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \neq 0$; any nonzero $f$ of order $0$ at all $P \in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and any $f$ in $R$'s valuation subring regular at all $P \in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$. Finally the sets $D_Q$ for distinct $Q \notin N$ are disjoint, the $q$-expansion image of $j$ has non-negative order at every $P \in D_Q$ for $Q \notin N$, and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R$'s valuation subring, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ` preserves $N$ and carries $D_Q$ to $D_{\tau \cdot Q}$ for $Q \notin N$, where the action on sets of places is $\{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_Q\}$.
--
--   This is the construction of the supersingular (Drinfeld) component of the semistable model of the full level-$q$ modular curve over $X_0(M')$ at a place above $q$, in the case $q = 2$ with an auxiliary rigidifying prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$: the component is presented as a regular prolongation of the valuation ring $A$ to the function field, together with $q+1$ distinguished ends and, away from them, étale charts over $A[X]$ with their residue discs, all equivariant for the level automorphisms over $\Gamma_0(M')$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularChart_local_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularChart_local_of_eq_two_of_dvd) to assemble the local chart data at the supersingular place $s$.
